{title: The LORD Reigns}
{subtitle: Psalms 97:1}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 77}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Abmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Cloud and thick darkness surround [Bb]him
[Cm]Righteousness and justice [Ab]are the foundation of his [Eb]throne
The world holds its breath in [Bb]awe
See the [Ab]King up[Bb]on the [Eb]throne [Bb/D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Cm]Fire goes before him on ev[Ab]ery side
[Cm]Consumes his foes in the burn[Ab]ing light
[Cm]No power can stand against [Ab]his might
The darkness flees before [Eb]the King
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The LORD reigns! Let the earth re[Bb]joice
Let the many [Cm]coastlands be [Ab]glad
His lightning [Eb]flashes light up the [Bb]world
The earth sees [Ab]and trembles in [Bb]his [Eb]hand
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Coastlands lift their voices [Bb]high
[Cm]Let the nations bow [Ab]before him now
[Eb]Justice stands where chaos [Bb]bowed
His throne [Ab]is built [Bb]on truth and [Eb]love [Bb/D]
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Pre-Chorus (repeat)}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The LORD reigns! Let the earth re[Bb]joice
Let the many [Cm]coastlands be [Ab]glad
His lightning [Eb]flashes light up the [Bb]world
The earth sees [Ab]and trembles in his [Bb][Eb]hand
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]Righteousness and [Bb]justice hold [Cm]him firm [Bb]
[Ab]The foundation [Bb]of his eter[Cm]nal rule [Bb]
[Ab]The [Bb]earth trembles at his [Cm]coming
[Bb]And [Ab]the coastlands [Bb]sing his [Eb]praise
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The LORD reigns! Let the earth re[Bb]joice
Let the many [Cm]coastlands be [Abmaj7]glad
His lightning [Eb]flashes light up the [Bb]world
The earth sees [Abmaj7]and trembles in [Bbsus4]his [Eb]hand
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The LORD reigns
Let the earth re[Bb]joice
{end_of_verse}

